  "source": { "doc": "mk75.pdf", "page": "8 and 9", "section": "Ordering Schematic Mark 75" },
  "note": "Extracted by hand from the ordering schematic, eighteen positions assembled bare. The actuator size digit runs through four positions, the range, the diaphragm, the actuator and the powered accessories, and the sheet prints the same 35M, 55M, 85M and 100M classes in each, so the digits are held consistent by constraints. The 100M class and the 8 inch size are printed for the side positioner model alone. The starred 3-9 and 9-15 ranges are positioner required, so on a plain 75 they refuse an empty SMP position. The seats section prints one ZZ spanning material and Cv, so a non-standard seat decodes as Z in each character, and the sheet's own line, consult factory for equal percentage requirements, is carried as a caution on the seat.",
